{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/reversed()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/reversed()"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"relatedModules":["Swift"],"name":"Cliques"}],"externalID":"s:STsE8reversedSay7ElementQzGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reversed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"extendedModule":"Swift","title":"reversed()","role":"symbol"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Inherited from "},{"code":"Sequence.reversed()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reversed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","title":"Cliques","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","kind":"symbol","title":"MaximalCliques","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/reversed()":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reversed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/reversed()","kind":"symbol","title":"reversed()","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/reversed()"}}}